<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Distance along a parallel</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(ix=1)"]]\(P(35^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 10^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\) and \(Q(35^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 48^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]\(P(50^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 15^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(50^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 30^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]\(P(20^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 65^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(20^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 20^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]\(P(60^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 25^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\) and \(Q(60^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 110^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]\(P(40^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 30^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(40^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 45^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]\(P(15^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 40^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\) and \(Q(15^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 95^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]\(P(55^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 12^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(55^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 38^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]\(P(25^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 70^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(25^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 15^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]\(P(65^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 5^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(65^\circ\,\mathrm{N}, 70^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]\(P(30^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 50^\circ\,\mathrm{W})\) and \(Q(30^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 20^\circ\,\mathrm{E})\)[[/if]] are on the same parallel of latitude. Take \(\pi = \tfrac{22}{7}\) and \(R = 6370\,\text{km}\). Distances in km within 0.1% of the exact value are accepted.</p><p>(a) Find the difference in longitude.</p><p>[[input:ans1]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the distance \(PQ\) along the parallel, to the nearest nautical mile.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] nm [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Find the distance \(PQ\) along the parallel, to the nearest km.</p><p>[[input:ans3]] km [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) [[if test="same"]]\(P\) and \(Q\) are on the same side of the Greenwich meridian, so subtract the longitudes.[[else]]\(P\) and \(Q\) are on opposite sides of the Greenwich meridian, so add the longitudes.[[/if]] [[if test="same"]]\(|{@l1@}^\circ - {@l2@}^\circ| = {@dl@}^\circ\).[[else]]\({@l1@}^\circ + {@l2@}^\circ = {@dl@}^\circ\).[[/if]]</p><p>(b) The parallel is a small circle of radius \(R\cos {@phi@}^\circ\): the same angle of longitude, on a smaller circle, so multiply by \(\cos {@phi@}^\circ\):</p><p>\[PQ = {@dl@} \times 60 \times \cos {@phi@}^\circ = {@dispdp(float(nm),1)@} \approx {@floor(nm+1/2)@} \text{ nm}.\]</p><p>(c) \[PQ = \frac{ {@dl@} }{360} \times 2 \times \frac{22}{7} \times 6370 \times \cos {@phi@}^\circ = {@dispdp(float(kmv),1)@} \approx {@floor(kmv+1/2)@}\,\text{km}.\]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
