  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Navigation: distance along a parallel</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.7 (c) / Essential 2.3 (d): Find the difference in longitude of two places on a parallel of latitude and the distance between them along the parallel in nautical miles and kilometres.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 3 (The sphere), Section 7, Example 2 and Exercise E, question 1 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: distance along a parallel in nautical miles; kilometres added, new positions.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
